  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(B)=0.3,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.7,$ find $P({A}^{\u2032}\\cup B).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.7 & =0.5+0.3-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.5+0.3-0.7 \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{\u2032}\\cup B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/14e573701578699d9c0fa5c0aa8f97d2c20fc916e867d0c89d3fe1256feccf69.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{\u2032}\\cup B)=0.1+0.2+0.3=0.6.\n$$",
